															"your User-Startup file. If it is already installed,\n"
															"you could of course skip this part of installation."))
	(set #writefifo							"\nWriting commandline in your User-Startup file:\n\n%s")
	(set #fileidlib							"\nNow copying FileID.Library...")
  (set #fileidlib_hlp	(cat		"The FileID.library will be used to identify the\n"
															"format of uploaded files. In fact of using this\n"
															"library, recognition errors (wrong extension i.e.)\n"
															"are now much less than only checking the extension\n"
															"This library is required for FAME to work!\n\n" @copylib-help))
	(set #xprzlib								"\nNow copying XprZModem.Library...")
	(set #xprzlib_hlp		(cat		"The XPRZModem.library is used to let users transfer\n"
															"files with the help of the Z-Modem protocol. This\n"
                              "library is not required, because FAME is able to\n"
															"control all XPR Transfer libraries, and therefor\n"
                              "it's your choice to install it or use other XPR-\n"
															"libraries instead.\n\n" @copylib-help))
	(set #shellstart		(cat		"Now copying the Start-Script for the internal\n"
															"FAME Shell into your S: directory under the name\n"
															"FAME-Startup."))
	(set #shellstarthlp (cat		"FAME-Startup will be used as Startscript for\n"
															"the internal Shell built into FAME. You could\n"
                              "define the Shell-Prompt, set some pathes etc.\n"
															"Further informations could be found in your\n"
															"Amiga-DOS manual."))
	(set #insertdisk1 (cat			"\nPlease insert the following disk\n"
															"in any drive:\n\n%s"))
	(set #insertdisk1help (cat	"You must now insert the according disk in any\n"
															"drive to continue with the installation.\n\n" @askdisk-help))
	(set #ERROR 								"\n%s aborted with errornumber %ld !")
	(set #ARCHIVE1			(cat		"\n\nNow extracting some important drawers and\n"
															"System-files to your FAME drawer.\n\n"
															"Depending on your processor-type it may take some\n"
															"time to extract the archive, i.e. a MC68000 CPU\n"
															"needs about 20 mins of extracting time !"))
	(set #ARCHIVE1HLP		(cat		"Installer will now extract some drawers and System-\n"
                              "files required by FAME to work into your FAME\n"
                              "drawer. Also some default settings are copied."))
	(set #ARCHIVE2							"\n\nExtracting and copying the main programs...")
	(set #ARCHIVE2HLP		(cat		"Installer copies now all main programs of FAME\n"
															"to your FAME-Drawer. Without those programs, FAME\n"
															"won't work !!!"))
	(set #englishdocu           "English Documentation")
	(set #germandocu						"German Documentation")
	(set #askformisc						"Please choose the additional Parts\nof FAME to install:")
	(set #askformischelp (cat		"The following parts may also installed:\n\n"
															"English Docu. - Latest Version of the\n"
		                          "                FAME-Documentation.\n"
                              "Archivers     - Contains the following archive-\n"
                              "                testers: ARJ, CheckExe, DMS, LHA\n"
															"                DMSDescript,EXEDescript,LZX,\n"
															"                mULTI-cHECK,TxtExtract,UNARJ,\n"
															"                UNZIP,ZoomCheck.\n\n"
                              "It's up to you to install them, at least you\n"
															"should install the Archivers to allow FAME\n"
															"to check all uploaded files !"))
	(set #EXTARCHIVE 			      "Extracting %s, please be patient...")
	(set #EXTARCHIVEHELP	(cat	"Selected archive will be extracted to your FAME\n"
															"drawer. A drawer for the according files will be\n"
                              "created."))
  (set #resprompt (cat				"Please choose the Parts of FAME which you want\n"
															"to load resident when starting the FAME:\n\n"
															"See 'Help...' for detailed informations !"))
	(set #resprompthlp (cat			"You where prompted to choose which parts of the\n"
															"FAME system should be loaded resident when starting\n"
															"FAME:\n\n"
															"MainPart        - Mainprogram of FAME, should be\n"
															"                  ALWAYS loaded resident !\n"
															"FAMEFileChecker - FAME FileCheck-Tool.\n"
                              "FAMEHydra       - The HydraTool of FAME.\n\n"
 															"Resident means that your choosen programs will be\n"
															"loaded into memory only one time. If the program\n"
															"will be started then more than one time, only copies\n"
															"of the program are returned instead of loading the\n"
															"program everytime new from disc. This saves memory\n"
															"and also increase the speed of FAME.\n"
															"To use this feature, you have to change all calls\n"
															"to those resident loadable programs by removing the\n"
															"path informations! Only the Filename remains, because\n"
															"AmigaDOS then searches first in the List of resident\n"
															"files before loading the file from disc. So make\n"
															"sure that you call resident programs only with their\n"
															"filename instead of using the whole path!\n\n"
                              "More about this could be found in your ADOS manual."))
	(set #writefile (cat				"\nWriting following line to file FAMEStart.bat:\n\n%s"))
	(set #writefilehelp (cat		"The line written above will be added to the script\n"
															"file called FAMEStart.bat. Detailed informations\n"
															"about this file could be found in the FAME docu-\n"
															"mentation."))
	(set #systeminfotext1 (cat	"\nInstaller now starts the SystemEditor of FAME.\n"
															"This program creates all missing datafiles and\n"
															"directories required to run FAME. After this, a\n"
															"window called \"SystemDatas\" appears and you\n"
															"must now configure your BBS into this window,\n"
                              "like the SysOp Name, BBSName, directory of the\n"
                              "user.datas etc."))
	(set #sysedstart1 (cat			"\nNow starting SystemEditor to configure\n"
															"the System datas of FAME..."))
	(set #askbatch 	(cat				"\nDo you want to install now two startscripts into\n"
															"directory FAME:NODE0/NODEBATCHES/LOGOFFBATCHES/\n"
															"to let 'LASTCALLERS' and 'MULTI-TOP' be started\n"
															"automatically after someone logs out ?\n\n"
															"See 'Help...' for further informations !"))
	(set #batchhelp (cat				"LastCallers and Multi-Top are FAME-Tools, which\n"
															"where started after an User logs out. If you\n"
